  "title": "Build a Microsoft Fabric Data Agent (Step by Step)",
  "description": "Yooo! \ud83d\ude4c take your data skills to the next level and join fellow data professionals in our community THE CUBE: https://guyinacube.com\n\nWhat if your report consumers could do more than browse reports? In this walkthrough, Marthe demonstrates how to build a Microsoft Fabric Data Agent that combines data from semantic models and lakehouses, adds business context through instructions, improves responses with example queries, validates results against Power BI, and securely shares the experience with users. You'll also see how Data Agents use DAX for semantic models, SQL for lakehouse queries, and how to access the agent with the Fabric Data Agent SDK and Azure AI solutions for enterprise-scale scenarios.\n\n\ud83d\udd17 LINKS\nFabric data agent concepts (preview): https://learn.microsoft.com/fabric/da...\n\n\u2705 KEY TAKEAWAYS\nCreate a Microsoft Fabric Data Agent from scratch.\nConnect semantic models and lakehouse tables as data sources.\nImprove agent accuracy with instructions, metadata, and example queries.\nValidate Data Agent responses by reviewing generated DAX and SQL queries.\nShare agents securely while respecting underlying data permissions.\nUse the Fabric Data Agent SDK and Azure AI integrations for custom applications.\n\n\ud83c\udfa5 RELATED VIDEOS\nMicrosoft Fabric Explained in less than 10 Minutes (Start Here): \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u2022\u00a0Microsoft\u00a0Fabric\u00a0Explained\u00a0in\u00a0less\u00a0than\u00a010...\u00a0\u00a0\nWhat is Microsoft Purview? Get the Overview and Unleash Data Governance with Purview & Fabric!: \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u2022\u00a0What\u00a0is\u00a0Microsoft\u00a0Purview?\u00a0Get\u00a0the\u00a0Overvie...\u00a0\u00a0\n\n\u23f1\ufe0f CHAPTERS\n00:00 Introduction to Microsoft Fabric Data Agents\n00:17 Why Data Agents Matter for Power BI Consumers\n01:00 Creating a New Data Agent\n01:25 Connecting Semantic Models and Lakehouse Data\n02:50 Teaching the Agent with Instructions\n04:06 Improving Results with Example Queries\n04:48 Testing Questions and Reviewing DAX Queries\n05:37 Advanced Analytics and Validation\n06:12 Publishing and Sharing the Agent\n07:00 Security and Data Permissions\n07:38 Using the Fabric Data Agent SDK with Python\n08:20 Azure AI and Enterprise Integration\n08:34 Final Thoughts and Use Cases\n\n\ud83c\udf10 LET'S CONNECT!\nOfficial website: https://guyinacube.com\nLinkedIn: \u00a0\u00a0/\u00a0guyinacube\u00a0\u00a0\nFacebook: \u00a0\u00a0/\u00a0guyinacube\u00a0\u00a0\nInstagram: \u00a0\u00a0/\u00a0guyinacube\u00a0\u00a0\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/guyinacube.com\nX: https://x.com/guyinacube\n\n\ud83c\udfa4 HOST\nMarthe Moengen\n\n#microsoftfabric #powerbi #ai #guyinacube",
